amux new — start a workgroup (no args: the create form)

usage: amux new ["<task>"] [flags]

Creates a workgroup and hands <task> to its coordinator, which starts the
member agents the task needs. With no repo the coordinator picks one or asks;
--repo limits the workgroup to those repos and seeds a first member on them
(idle until the coordinator steers it). With no arguments at all, the
interactive create form opens (needs a terminal).

Coordinators are interactive and members run as tasks; --interactive is the
advanced override for that first member.

flags:
  --repo <name>                (repeatable) limit the workgroup to this tracked repo and seed a first member on it
                               (repeat, or give a comma list)
  --harness <harness>          the first member's harness: claude | codex (default: claude)
  --model <model>              the first member's model (default: the harness's default)
  --coordinator <harness>      the coordinator's harness: claude | codex (default: codex)
  --coordinator-model <model>  the coordinator's model
  --name <name>                workgroup display name
  --interactive                advanced: the first member is interactive instead of a task

examples:
  amux new
  amux new "upgrade CI to Go 1.26"
  amux new "fix the flaky auth test" --repo api --harness codex
